    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q1",
      "question": "<p>A system of three equations is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"kx + 3y - z = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3x - y + z = -k\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-16x - ky - kz = k\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><p>Given that there is no unique solution to all three equations,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k = 2\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k = 2\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) determine whether the three equations are consistent, justifying your answer.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Interpret the answer to part (b) geometrically.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
