      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q3",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:85mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q03-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. The upper semicircle is shaded.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a circle with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> and centre at the origin. The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 1, is bounded by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the part of the circle for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y &gt; 0\"></span>. The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis to create a sphere with volume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span>.</p><p>Use integration to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
