    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q5",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:85mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. A rectangular block with all three dimensions labelled.\"></figure><p>A block has length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(r + 2)\"></span> cm, width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(r + 1)\"></span> cm and height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> cm, as shown in Figure 2.</p><p>In a set of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> such blocks, the first block has a height of 1 cm, the second block has a height of 2 cm, the third block has a height of 3 cm and so on.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^3, \\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\"></span> to show that the total volume, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span>, of all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> blocks in the set is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V = \\frac{n}{4} (n + 1)(n + 2)(n + 3) \\quad n \\geqslant 1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>Given that the total volume of all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> blocks is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(n^4 + 6n^3 - 11710) \\text{ cm}^3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) determine how many blocks make up the set.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
