    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q6",
      "question": "<p>(i)</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 &amp; a \\\\ a - 4 &amp; b \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are non-zero constants.</p><p>Given that the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}\"></span> is self-inverse,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and the possible values for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}\"></span> represents a linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>.</p><p>Using the smaller value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> from part (a),</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) show that the invariant points of the linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span> form a line, stating the equation of this line.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(ii)</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{P} = \\begin{pmatrix} p &amp; 2p \\\\ -1 &amp; 3p \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{P}\"></span> represents a linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span>.</p><p>The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> has vertices at the points with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1, 2), (3, 2)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2, 5)\"></span>.</p><p>The area of the image of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> under the linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> is 15</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> consists of a stretch scale factor 3 parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis invariant followed by a stretch scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\"></span> parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis invariant. The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{Q}\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Write down the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{Q}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> followed by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>, which is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{R}\"></span>,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{R}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
