    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2020-october/q7",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(z) = z^4 + az^3 + bz^2 + cz + d\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b, c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>The equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z) = 0\"></span> has complex roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1, z_2, z_3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_4\"></span>.</p><p>When plotted on an Argand diagram, the points representing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1, z_2, z_3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_4\"></span> form the vertices of a square, with one vertex in each quadrant.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1 = 2 + 3i\"></span>, determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b, c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
